status GREEN -- awk_lcg_exact at overflowing=0 unread=17 with its control tracked, 57 legs 0 failing; torus_fold 28 and workload_trial 62 re-proven on the moved generator; reds_ledger_monotone, reds_fold, reds_citation, reds_shelf_resolve, reds_spine_derive, unshared_citation and reds_pin_capacity GREEN on metal. Named honestly: the cold endurance run was PARTIAL -- 78 of ~400 guards under eight ships' contention, 77 green and one red, rune_assert_sweep, a peer's ratchet the card already records; standing_equipment reds on 16 recorded run states belonging to peer lanes, and it refused before my roster row as well as after, checked both ways. standing_equipment_redleg reads guards_no_refusal_marker=52 against a ceiling of 51, and that is NOT mine either -- my witness carries the _control.sh spelling, and the count reads 52 with my roster row stashed away as well as with it in place, checked both ways.
recommend keep-going -- a lap's own round-open output is the second surface no guard reaches, and BAKERY booked the same shape today; whether a loop should be made to READ its own stash back at the open is worth one lane's design round.
